            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a new method for obtaining user-friendly, robust pattern electroretinograms (PERG) simultaneously from each eye using asynchronous binocular stimulation and one-channel acquisition of signals recorded from a subcutaneous needle in the snout.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
